   "source": "thehindu.com",
   "published": "Sat, 07 Nov 2026 21:53:47 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794068627.0,
   "ageDays": 0.06,
   "summary": "Venugopal has said that Chief Election Commissioner (CEC) Gyanesh Kumar would soon be forced to step down. Inaugurating the ‘Vote Bachao, Desh Bachao’ (Save the Vote, Save the Nation) rally organised by the Kozhikode District Congress Committee at Kozhikode beach on Saturday (November 7, 2026), Mr. Venugopal accused Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Union Home Minister Amit Shah of using the Election Commission of India to undermine the Congress and manipulate electoral outcomes.",
   "summary_zh": "韦努戈帕尔表示，首席选举专员（CEC）贾内什·库马尔很快将被迫下台。11月7日星期六，韦努戈帕尔先生为科泽科德县国大党委员会在科泽科德海滩组织的“守护选票，守护国家”（Save the Vote, Save the Nation）集会揭幕，指责印度总理纳伦德拉·莫迪和联邦内政部长阿米特·沙阿利用印度选举委员会削弱国大党并操纵选举结果。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Amid the Opposition’s intensifying protests over alleged electoral malpractice, All India Congress Committee (AICC) general secretary K.C. Venugopal has said that Chief Election Commissioner (CEC) Gyanesh Kumar would soon be forced to step down. Inaugurating the ‘Vote Bachao, Desh Bachao’ (Save the Vote, Save the Nation) rally organised by the Kozhikode District Congress Committee at Kozhikode beach on Saturday (November 7, 2026), Mr. Venugopal accused Prime Minister Narendra Modi and Union Home Minister Amit Shah of using the Election Commission of India to undermine the Congress and manipulate electoral outcomes. Referring to the Haryana Assembly election, in which the Congress lost by a margin of 0.4 percentage points despite predictions of a party wave, he said a booth-level investigation led by Rahul Gandhi had exposed large-scale vote theft. Similar manipulation had allegedly taken place in Maharashtra and Karnataka, he claimed. Mr. Venugopal levelled serious allegations against Mr. Kumar, accusing him of corruption during his earlier stints as Ernakulam District Collector and Public Works department Secretary in Kerala. He also alleged that Mr. Kumar had been entrusted with overseeing the bifurcation of Jammu and Kashmir by Mr. Shah. Criticising the 2023 amendment to the law governing the appointment of election commissioners, he alleged that the Modi government had granted them legal immunity even greater than that enjoyed by the President, Prime Minister, and Chief Justice of India. He also accused the government of removing the Chief Justice of India from the selection committee and replacing him with a Union Minister, despite a Supreme Court judgment providing for the CJI's inclusion. Claiming that 13.32 crore voters had been deleted from electoral rolls across the country, Mr. Venugopal said the exercise threatened not only citizens’ voting rights but also their access to government benefits and entitlements, as voter ID cards were increasingly being linked to welfare provisions. He said the protests in Delhi had unsettled the Prime Minister and the CEC, and warned that any attempt to suppress the agitation using the police or armed forces would invite a strong response from the Opposition. The movement was not merely about electoral victories or making Mr. Gandhi Prime Minister in 2029, but a fight to safeguard every Indian citizen's right to vote and democratic freedoms, he added. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
