   "title": "Makinde: Tinubu’s poor planning plunged millions of Nigerians into hardship",
   "url": "https://www.vanguardngr.com/2026/11/makinde-tinubus-poor-planning-plunged-millions-of-nigerians-into-hardship/",
   "domain": "vanguardngr.com",
   "source": "vanguardngr.com",
   "published": "Sat, 07 Nov 2026 13:13:04 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794057184.0,
   "ageDays": 0.19,
   "summary": "Oyo State Governor and presidential candidate of the Allied Peoples Movement (APM), Seyi Makinde, has blamed the economic hardship facing millions of Nigerians on what he described as inadequate planning by the President Bola Tinubu-led administration. Makinde said major economic policy decisions introduced by the Federal Government were implemented without adequate plans and frameworks to cushion their effects on citizens, thereby worsening the economic difficulties faced by Nigerians.",
   "summary_zh": "奥约州州长、联合人民运动（APM）总统候选人塞伊·马金德将数百万尼日利亚人面临的经济困境归咎于他所说的博拉·蒂努布总统领导的政府规划不足。马金德表示，联邦政府推出的重大经济政策在缺乏充分计划和框架的情况下便付诸实施，未能减轻这些政策对公民造成的影响，从而加剧了尼日利亚人面临的经济困难。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Oyo State Governor and presidential candidate of the Allied Peoples Movement (APM), Seyi Makinde, has blamed the economic hardship facing millions of Nigerians on what he described as inadequate planning by the President Bola Tinubu-led administration. Makinde said major economic policy decisions introduced by the Federal Government were implemented without adequate plans and frameworks to cushion their effects on citizens, thereby worsening the economic difficulties faced by Nigerians. The APM presidential candidate spoke on Friday during a live interview on the Bauchi Radio Corporation (BRC), while in Bauchi State to flag off his 2027 presidential campaign. He argued that the immediate impact of the administration’s economic policies on Nigerians was a consequence of taking major decisions without adequate preparation and effective implementation strategies. Makinde stressed that economic reforms must be supported by proper planning and clear implementation frameworks to ensure that ordinary citizens do not bear the brunt of government policies. He said addressing the country’s economic challenges would require fundamental structural reforms and strong political will. The Oyo governor also highlighted the APM’s Reset Nigeria Agenda, which he said was designed to address the country’s challenges through a documented policy framework and the party’s manifesto. According to him, the agenda focuses on reforming critical sectors of the economy, promoting sustainable development and restoring true federalism that recognises and respects Nigeria’s diverse nationalities. Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "ng"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol",
    "eco"
   ],
   "tier": 3,
   "actor": "当事国政府",
   "alsoUS": false,
   "cnHit": false,
