   "published": "Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:52:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793890323.0,
   "ageDays": 2.12,
   "summary": "Korea's key financial policymakers on Thursday vowed to closely monitor potential changes in U.S. policies on artificial intelligence (AI) and trade and their implications for the Korean economy. Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il discussed the issues with Bank of Korea (BOK) Gov. Shin Hyun-song, Financial Services Commission Chairman Lee Eog-weon and Financial Supervisory Service Gov. Lee Chan-jin after the U.S. Democratic Party secured a huge win in the midterm elections this week.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国主要金融政策制定者周四誓言，将密切监测美国人工智能和贸易政策可能发生的变化及其对韩国经济的影响。在美国民主党本周于中期选举中取得压倒性胜利后，韩国财政部长李亨烈与韩国银行行长申铉松、金融服务委员会主席李恩元、金融监督服务院长李(chan)-jin讨论了这些问题。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea's key financial policymakers on Thursday vowed to closely monitor potential changes in U.S. policies on artificial intelligence (AI) and trade and their implications for the Korean economy. Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il discussed the issues with Bank of Korea (BOK) Gov. Shin Hyun-song, Financial Services Commission Chairman Lee Eog-weon and Financial Supervisory Service Gov. Lee Chan-jin after the U.S. Democratic Party secured a huge win in the midterm elections this week. During the meeting, the officials noted that despite gains in major stock markets in the United States and Europe, concerns over tighter regulation of the AI industry had led to declines in semiconductor shares. The participants exchanged views on possible changes in Washington's fiscal, trade and industrial policies following the election outcome and vowed to closely keep tabs on policy and the regulatory environment, as well as U.S. tariffs and developments in the Middle East war. \"The officials agreed to step up efforts to promote stable growth of the Korean economy by addressing changes in the external environment through close coordination among relevant organizations and thoroughly preparing for a possible increase in financial market volatility,\" the finance ministry said",
